  "notes": "{愛|あい}する is a formal/literary way to say \"to love.\"\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: ⟦{他動詞|たどうし}→他動詞：10418_tadoushi⟧ (transitive)\n- No standard intransitive pair\n- Pattern: [noun]⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{愛|あい}する\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {愛|あい}する: to love (formal/literary)\n- ⟦{大好|だいす}き→大好き：02911_daisuki⟧: to love/like very much (casual)\n- ⟦{好|す}き→好き：02355_suki⟧: to like\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- ⟦{愛|あい}→愛：02370_ai⟧: love (noun)\n- ⟦{愛情|あいじょう}→愛情：01673_aijou⟧: affection\n- ⟦{恋|こい}→恋：02208_koi⟧: romantic love\n- ⟦{恋愛|れんあい}→恋愛：12634_renai⟧: romance\n\nNote: {愛|あい}する is often used in songs, poetry, and formal contexts. In everyday speech, ⟦{大好|だいす}き→大好き：02911_daisuki⟧ is more common.\n\nASPECT (ている):\n- {愛|あい}して⟦いる→いる：00495_iru⟧: loves, is in love with (stative — describes a continuing emotional state, not an action)\n- Note: The て⟦いる→いる：00495_iru⟧ form is the standard way to express 'love' as a current feeling. ⟦{彼|かれ}→彼：01292_kare⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{愛|あい}して⟦います→いる：00495_iru⟧ = 'I love him.' The plain form {愛|あい}する by itself is mainly used in literary writing, song lyrics, and relative clauses like {愛|あい}する⟦{人|ひと}→人：00476_hito⟧ ('the person I love'). Learners should use {愛|あい}して⟦いる→いる：00495_iru⟧ when stating they currently love someone.",
